---
// How the clabernetes provider captures a node interface: the clabwire sidecar captures, Antimony reads it via exec.
---

<figure class="diagram">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 720 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="cap-c9s-title cap-c9s-desc">
		<title id="cap-c9s-title">Packet capture with clabernetes</title>
		<desc id="cap-c9s-desc">
			The Antimony server runs outside the cluster. Through the Kubernetes API server, it runs the capture tool of the
			clabwire sidecar in the node's pod with pods/exec. The sidecar captures one of the node's link interfaces and
			sends the pcap stream back through the API server. Each run lasts at most one hour and Antimony starts the next.
		</desc>
		<defs>
			<marker id="cap-c9s-aa" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="arrow-accent" />
			</marker>
			<marker id="cap-c9s-aw" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="arrow-warm" />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<!-- Antimony server -->
		<rect x="20" y="70" width="170" height="96" rx="10" class="box-accent" />
		<text x="36" y="96" class="t">Antimony server</text>
		<text x="36" y="114" class="t-sub">outside the cluster</text>
		<text x="36" y="144" class="t-mono">chains 1 h runs</text>
		<text x="36" y="158" class="t-mono">into one stream</text>

		<!-- Cluster -->
		<rect x="240" y="20" width="460" height="190" rx="14" class="zone" />
		<text x="256" y="44" class="t-zone">Kubernetes cluster</text>

		<rect x="260" y="80" width="120" height="76" rx="10" class="box" />
		<text x="276" y="106" class="t">API server</text>
		<text x="276" y="126" class="t-mono">pods/exec</text>

		<rect x="420" y="56" width="264" height="140" rx="10" class="box" />
		<text x="436" y="80" class="t">Node pod</text>
		<rect x="436" y="92" width="232" height="50" rx="8" class="box-warm" />
		<text x="452" y="113" class="t">clabwire sidecar</text>
		<text x="452" y="131" class="t-sub">captures the node's link interfaces</text>
		<rect x="436" y="150" width="232" height="34" rx="8" class="box" />
		<text x="452" y="172" class="t-sub">Node container</text>

		<path d="M190 100 H256" class="edge-accent" marker-end="url(#cap-c9s-aa)" />
		<text x="204" y="92" class="t-mono">exec</text>
		<path d="M380 106 H432" class="edge-accent" marker-end="url(#cap-c9s-aa)" />
		<path d="M432 128 H384" class="edge-warm" marker-end="url(#cap-c9s-aw)" />
		<path d="M256 138 H194" class="edge-warm" marker-end="url(#cap-c9s-aw)" />
		<text x="204" y="156" class="t-mono">pcap</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>
		The sidecar wires the node's links, so it can capture them. The management interface isn't one of them.
	</figcaption>
</figure>
